Description: Qualify the Fortran test compiler for nocheck builds
 Debian rules already set make_check=no for cross or nocheck builds. The
 C libltdl build does not require a target Fortran compiler. Keep the compiler
 dependency for checked builds instead of making C-library bootstrap depend
 on a missing SPE Fortran toolchain. No target Fortran validation is claimed.
Author: Tabor port contributors
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-03

--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 Source: libtool
 Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
   file,
-  gfortran | fortran95-compiler,
+  gfortran <!nocheck> | fortran95-compiler <!nocheck>,
   automake (>= 1:1.14.1-3),
   autoconf (>= 2.69-7),
   help2man,
